From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Connor Buchan <mikey@blindcomputing.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 20:05:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: kindle3: stop autoboot and service the watchdog

The recovery image is loaded entirely into RAM to provide an interactive USB
console. Stop at that console instead of booting an entry from the internal
eMMC.

Amazon's preceding boot stage leaves the i.MX watchdog running. Enable the
normal Barebox watchdog poller without changing its inherited timeout so a
healthy recovery session remains available.

Upstream: Not submitted (recovery-image policy)
Signed-off-by: Michael Connor Buchan <mikey@blindcomputing.org>
---
 arch/arm/boards/kindle3/kindle3.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boards/kindle3/kindle3.c
+++ b/arch/arm/boards/kindle3/kindle3.c
@@ -198,6 +198,14 @@ static const iomux_v3_cfg_t kindle3_pads[] = {
 
 static int kindle3_part_init(void)
 {
+	struct device_d *watchdog;
+
+	set_autoboot_state(AUTOBOOT_ABORT);
+
+	watchdog = get_device_by_name("wdog0");
+	if (watchdog)
+		dev_set_param(watchdog, "autoping", "1");
+
 	devfs_add_partition("disk0", SZ_1K, 2 * SZ_1K,
 			    DEVFS_PARTITION_FIXED, "disk0.imx_header");
 	devfs_add_partition("disk0", 4 * SZ_1K, (192 - 1) * SZ_1K,
-- 
